{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1188136-merits-that-add-dots-to-other-merits","id":1188136,"title":"Merits that add Dots to other Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-21T05:16:04-08:00","id":1188136,"title":"Merits that add Dots to other Merits","content":"So lets say you have 4 dots of Resources.<br /> And then you get the <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Invested </span></span></span></div>\u200bInvictus Merit - lets say you are Status 1.<br /> <br /> \u200bCan you just add 4+1 = 5 and always have 5 dots of Resources?<br /> <br /> \u200bOr its a different income so you have the 4 dot of yours and one dot of Resources from the Covenant?<br /> <br /> \u200bSame thing goes with other merits as Carthian Pull","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12248-kafrospaladin","name":"kafrospaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:25:28-08:00","id":1188139,"title":"","content":"&quot;These dots can be added to existing Merit dots...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, yes. It can work like that. With ST approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:42:51-08:00","id":1188146,"title":"","content":"Seems kinda lame to me. Especially if you think that the covenants borrow you or give you staff, so why should it be added to your existing dots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12248-kafrospaladin","name":"kafrospaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:49:44-08:00","id":1188149,"title":"","content":"Well, in the case of Resources you can imagine a Covenant being more willing to provide a large sum of Resources to someone who already has quite a large bankaccount. They will come across as more trustworthy when it comes to managing finances.<br /> <br /> Remember, too, that the Drawback to the merit is that the Covenant scrutinizes your behaviour closely. These extra merit dots may be given freely from a mechanical perspective, they are not from a narrative perspective. An Invictus member who'd blow his fifth dot of Resources on investing in an obvious pyramid scheme would quickly be stripped of those extra funds (and probably of a few dots of Status too). The underlying assumption is, I think, that the extra dots are put to use in a manner that benefits the Covenant as a whole.<br /> <br /> EDIT: an extra dot of Retainer could be narrated as that Retainer undergoing training or perhaps getting better equipment. There's always some angle to justify the loss or gaining of merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:46:23-08:00","id":1188184,"title":"","content":"With resources part of it probably comes down to investment opitunites, if you can only manage to scrape together one dot on your own then they'll tell you to invest in certain companies that they plan on bumping the stock price up or give you a better price on the supplies your buissness requires, if you have four dots they'll take the time to get your fingers into all the pies as long as you're willing to extend the same courtesy to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T14:34:58-08:00","id":1189469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kafrospaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1188136-merits-that-add-dots-to-other-merits?p=1188146#post1188146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems kinda lame to me. Especially if you think that the covenants borrow you or give you staff, so why should it be added to your existing dots</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons I would agree with that sentiment is that in the game, one dot of resources is a step above a basic income, whereas five is upper crust spending. Now, say you are 'invested' in a group with four of your friends, each with one dot. They lend their merit power to you, and boon, you go from just scraping by to winning at life. That...doesn't feel right at all. This non-liner growth and the mathematics surrounding it has annoyed me in the past. That said, it is super minor and doesn't break the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:09:18-07:00","id":1194824,"title":"","content":"It has to be justified within the fiction. Think of the Invictus as a big corporation and you are a trustworthy employee, you can draw a sum of money from them as long as they know that it will be used for the better benefit of the Covenant (and yourself but that comes second) the money is still tied to the Invictus however and they can cut your funding as soon as it proves to be more of a detriment than a benefit to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T04:35:03-07:00","id":1197553,"title":"","content":"So no buying hookers and Changeling Blood with it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T04:50:59-07:00","id":1197559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1188136-merits-that-add-dots-to-other-merits?p=1197553#post1197553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no buying hookers and Changeling Blood with it</div> </div> </div> </div>You can if those hookers and changeling blood can be written off as a business expense that ensures a client pursues business with the corporation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:12:12-07:00","id":1197609,"title":"","content":"Resources is not just how much money you make. It is also about your ability to obtain things at your resource level. It's about your disposable income. I am almost positive it's not about investments, because then your money is all tied up and you have no disposable income.<br /> <br /> You could be living in some beautiful mansion and drive a rolls, AND have 0 resources. It would just indicate that every last penny you make goes into paying all your bills, thus having zero disposable income. <br /> <br /> So with this an adding the 5th dot to your already owned 4, is pretty reasonable. Maybe your people allow you to use their private jet whenever you want, or use the company card to make purchases there are lots of ways to justify it other than suddenly getting paychecks from these people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:57:01-07:00","id":1197653,"title":"","content":"That's a very good point, given how abstract resources is it's probably a lot of different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T13:51:49-07:00","id":1197732,"title":"","content":"Invested is just the name of merit which indicates your are invested with the Invictus (not necessarily financially). You can choose for the status dots to go into any of the merits listed, not just resources. Resources does not reflect your financial investments, it reflects your disposal income. An exact dollar amount isn't given because it will be different depending on chronicle and location - you just get to procure items once per chapter. So for the OP's example if you had Resources 4, Invested, and Status (Invictus) 1 and you chose Resources - once per story you could pull out an item valued for Resources 5 (or lower) without any issue - that is all it does mechanically.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, story-wise you could put a number of different spins on it. Your political enemies in the Invictus could point out what you are doing with those merits or otherwise try to block you from using it. And of course a storyteller may have additional notes on using it, but IMO if you are paying for the merit you should be able to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}